includes: INSERT FX (new): each drum channel now has its own insert effect in the Channel Rack — a resonant Filter (low-pass / high-pass / off) with Cutoff, plus Drive (soft saturation). Per-channel, persisted, applied to BOTH the sample and synth-drum voices so it works in any pad mode (audio-thread-reviewed, unit-tested DSP core). CHANNEL RACK: Tools ▸ Editors ▸ Channels opens a per-track mixer — each drum channel has its Level, plus Mute and Solo (and Clear Solo). Muted channels stay silent; soloing focuses just the soloed channels; rows dim to show what's audible. State persists; manual pad taps still always sound. TOP BAR: a persistent brand header is now always on screen in every view (Arrange · Clips · Compose) — "Echoelmusic" is CENTRED, with the E-with-waves app mark on the left and the running version/build on the right, so you always know which build you're on. Builds on v10.35.1 with device-log fixes. CALMER EVOLUTION: the bio composition was re-rolling every ~2-4 s and never settled — the auto-evolve cadence is now ~4 bars (8-16 s) with a 6 s anti-flood floor, so the take hugs the live body but is given room to breathe into a phrase (your manual edits stay instant). rPPG RE-GRIP FIX: right after you re-placed your finger, motion settling could peak-count a harmonic and lock a false-high BPM (~180 at rest) for ~20 s; a fresh lock is now cross-checked against the independent autocorrelation period and rejected if it disagrees >20 % — steady tracking is untouched. BRIGHTER/LIVELIER DEFAULT TONE: every genre patch is voiced a touch brighter (brightness +0.10, upper-partial body +0.05), modest + uniform + clamped so each genre keeps its character — one reversible lever to tune after you A/B on device. Plus everything from v10.35.1: persistent bottom nav + structured collapsible Tools panel, PPQ note precision, AutomationLane foundation, felt sub + missing-fundamental, envelope-tracking spectral visual. All Xcode-Compile-Check green per commit. Still honestly held for a dedicated cycle: unison/detune richness (additive-engine CPU design) + per-track insert FX + multi-track arrangement.
